* A program that is only the program: the vocabulary comes from a library.
*
* `@include` reads another file's declarations here. The path is relative to
* this file, so where the command is run from cannot change what it means, and
* a file included twice is read once, which is what lets two libraries share a
* third without either of them knowing. Nothing here needs that -- this file
* names one library, which names one more -- but `lib/fast.bfm` and
* `lib/wide.bfm` both include `lib/idioms.bfm`, so a program wanting both gets
* it once.

@include "lib/idioms.bfm"

@var out

@say(out, 'h')
@say(out, 'i')
@newline(out)
